### 7.4 Individual-fold crossings: exhaustive ledger

There are **144 qualifying individual fold/method/seed runs** among the 540 saved primary runs. A repeated-CV test fold contains only 7–13 real samples, so a small number of changed decisions can move BA substantially. No LOCO or cross-study-transfer fold crosses 80.00%. These are not 144 independent successes or 144 newly validated cohorts. Fold crossings are retained below even when their matched baseline is better or their overall protocol mean is below 80.00%.

Every ledger row uses **LDA, 50 CpGs and threshold 0.5**. Run IDs encode the complete dataset/cohort/protocol, repeat, fold, method and seed; `GSE99511_cv` is secondary within-GSE99511 CV, `GSE46306_strict_cv` is strict primary CV, and `GSE46306_reconciled_cv` is the sensitivity CV. The run ID links to its prediction file. The baseline BA links to the exact same-fold real-only prediction file. Corresponding metric JSONs have the identical stem under [outputs/metrics/primary](outputs/metrics/primary/). Config: [protocol.yaml](configs/protocol.yaml). TP/TN/FP/FN and additional metrics in the ledger refer only to that row's real held-out fold.

